[{"category":"section","location":"#InteractiveMPI","page":"Home","text":"Documentation for InteractiveMPI.\n\n","title":"InteractiveMPI"},{"category":"type","location":"#InteractiveMPI.MPIBackend","page":"Home","text":"abstract type MPIBackend end\n\nParent type for MPI backends. Instances of such types are passed to start.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InteractiveMPI.MPIBackend"},{"category":"type","location":"#InteractiveMPI.ThreadsMPIBackend","page":"Home","text":"backend = ThreadsMPIBackend(size)\n\nReturn backend to be passed as second argument to start.  This backend uses Julia threads instead of the MPI module.  start will spawn size threads that act as size MPI processes.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InteractiveMPI.ThreadsMPIBackend"},{"category":"type","location":"#InteractiveMPI.TrueMPIBackend","page":"Home","text":"backend = TrueMPIBackend()\n\nReturn backend::MPIBackend to be passed as second argument to start. MPI invocations are then passed through to the MPI module. Use this for production runs. This backend is fully functional only if the Julia MPI module is loaded by the main script or a project dependency:\n\nimport MPI\n...\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InteractiveMPI.TrueMPIBackend"},{"category":"function","location":"#InteractiveMPI.Critical","page":"Home","text":"result = MPI.Critical(fun::Function)\n\nReturn fun() in a thread-safe way.  Calls to thread-unsafe external libraries (like NetCDF) can be wrapped in a do-block:\n\nresult = MPI.Critical() do\n    ... # thread-unsafe code\nend\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InteractiveMPI.Critical"},{"category":"function","location":"#InteractiveMPI.start","page":"Home","text":"InteractiveMPI.start(main, backend::MPIBackend, args...)\n\nInvoke function main according to backend. main accepts as first argument an object MPI  to be used as if it were the Julia MPI module. Extra arguments args... are passed to main after MPI.\n\nfunction main(MPI, args...)\n    # use the object `MPI` as if it were the module `MPI`\n    MPI.Init()\n    comm = MPI.COMM_WORLD\n    rank = MPI.Comm_rank(comm)\n    ...\nend\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InteractiveMPI.start"}]
